WEBVTT

00:45.708 --> 00:49.689
I can see the blue from a million miles away.

00:53.431 --> 00:57.573
I can see the storms where we used to stay.

01:00.454 --> 01:04.876
In the silence of the vacuum, the air is

01:04.956 --> 01:11.597
perfectly still. But my shoulders remember the

01:11.637 --> 01:12.578
heavy hill

01:16.240 --> 01:19.282
I'm floating in the velvet, I'm drifting in the

01:19.382 --> 01:23.745
night But my hand still breaks for the sudden

01:23.905 --> 01:24.385
fight

01:27.888 --> 01:31.390
It's a phantom gravity pulling at my mind

01:31.410 --> 01:35.953
Tethered to the world that I left behind

01:38.265 --> 01:43.107
And I still feel the anchor's weight Even when

01:43.127 --> 01:48.629
the chains are gone I still feel the hands of fate

01:50.069 --> 01:56.211
Pushing me to carry on It doesn't hold me down It

01:56.311 --> 02:00.993
doesn't drag me deep But it's a memory The metal

02:01.013 --> 02:06.755
wants to keep The anchor's weight

02:13.812 --> 02:16.856
The flashes in the courtroom, the yelling in the

02:16.937 --> 02:20.682
hall, I watch it like a movie projected on the

02:20.762 --> 02:24.146
wall. The fire doesn't burn me, the friction

02:24.286 --> 02:27.110
isn't real, but the ghost of the pressure is

02:27.250 --> 02:31.934
something I can feel. We cut the line and fired up

02:32.034 --> 02:35.936
the drive But the echo of the cage is keeping it

02:35.956 --> 02:40.498
alive It's a phantom gravity pulling at my mind A

02:40.638 --> 02:47.401
tether to the world that I left behind

02:47.521 --> 02:52.283
I still feel the anchor's weight Even when the

02:52.383 --> 02:57.585
chains are gone I still feel the hands of fate

02:59.095 --> 03:05.241
Pushing me to carry on It doesn't hold me down It

03:05.341 --> 03:10.426
doesn't drive me deep But it's a memory The metal

03:10.446 --> 03:15.771
wants to keep The anchors light

03:46.317 --> 03:49.619
I don't need to fight it, I don't need to run I'm

03:49.679 --> 03:53.701
standing in the light of a different sun The

03:53.821 --> 03:58.643
metal is cold, the sanctuary is clear I am the

03:58.923 --> 04:10.009
anchor And I am safe out here

04:10.109 --> 04:14.812
I still feel the anchor's weight Even when the

04:14.892 --> 04:20.475
chains are gone I still feel the hands of fate

04:21.615 --> 04:27.778
Pushing me to carry on It doesn't hold me down It

04:27.898 --> 04:32.940
doesn't drag me deep But it's a memory The metal

04:32.980 --> 04:42.284
wants to keep The anchors weighed Safe out here

04:44.697 --> 04:49.738
phantom gravity he anchors away

